  "live_records": {
    "q-80346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80346",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the set $X=\\{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24\\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\{6,12,18\\},\\{15,21\\},\\,____\\,\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $3$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $6\\in \\{6,12,18\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $12\\in \\{6,12,18\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $15\\in \\{15,21\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $18\\in \\{6,12,18\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $21\\in \\{15,21\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $24$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $3,$ $9,$ and $24$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{3,9,24\\}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
