    "q-105868": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105868",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the set $X=\\{0,1,2,3,…,10\\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\{2,3,5,7\\},\\{0,1\\},\\,\\{4,8\\},\\,____\\,\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $0\\in \\{0,1\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\in \\{0,1\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $2\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $3\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\in \\{4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $6$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}$\n\n- $8\\in \\{4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $10$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $6,9,$ and $10$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{6,9,10\\}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
