    "q-81126": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81126",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the set $D=\\{f,g,h,i,j,k,l,m\\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $D?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\{f,h\\},\\{j,l\\},\\{k,m\\},\\,____\\,\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $D$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $D$ where every element of $D$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $D$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $D$ and check:\n\n- $f\\in \\{f,h\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $g$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $h\\in \\{f,h\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $i$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $j\\in \\{j,l\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $k\\in \\{k,m\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $l\\in \\{j,l\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $m\\in \\{k,m\\}\\,✓$\n\nThe elements $g$ and $i$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{g,i\\}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
