    "q-81135": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81135",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "If $C=\\{20,25,30,35,40,45\\},$ which collection of subsets of $C$ is a partition of $C?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $C$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $C$ where every element of $C$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{20\\},\\{25,30\\},\\{35,40,45\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{20\\},\\{25,30\\},\\{35,40,45\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- $\\{\\{20,25,30\\},\\{25,35,40,45\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $25$ appears in two subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{20,30\\},\\{25,35,30\\},\\{20,30,40,45\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the elements $20$ and $30$ appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{20,25,30,35,45\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $40\\in C$ does not appear in any subset.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81135-a",
