      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "If $A=\\{0,10,20,…,900\\},$ which collection of subsets of $A$ is a partition of $A?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{0\\},\\{10,20,30,…,900\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{0,10,20,…,900\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- $\\{\\{10,30,50…,890\\},\\{20,40,60,…,900\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $0$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,10,20,…,890\\}\\},\\{20,40,60,…,900\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $20,40,60,…,900,$ that appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{10,30,50…,890\\}\\},\\{0,20,40,60,…,800\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the elements $820,840…,900$ do not appear in any subsets.",
