    "q-105888": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105888",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "If $Y=\\{1,2,3,…,100\\},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,100\\},\\{1,3,5,…,99\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,100\\},\\{5,15,25…,95\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $1$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{2,4,6,…,40\\},\\{1,2,3,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $2$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,1,2,3,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains the element $0$ that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{1,2,3,…,100\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
