      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "If $A=\\{0,3,6,…,99\\},$ which collection of subsets of $A$ is a partition of $A?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{0,6,12…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{0,3,6,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,12,24…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $6$) that do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,1,2,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition  is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $1$) that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- $\\{\\{0,3,6…,96\\},\\{3,9,15,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the elements $3,9,15,…,93$ appear in multiple subsets.",
