    "q-80432": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80432",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "If $X=\\{1,3,5,…,99\\}$, which collection of subsets of $X$ is a partition of $X?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,99\\},\\{2,4,6,…,98\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,49\\},\\{41,43,45,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,69\\},\\{70,71,72,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because it contains many even elements (such as $70$) that do not appear in $X.$\n\n- $\\{\\{1,3,5,…,39\\},\\{51,53,55,…,99\\}\\}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $41$) do not appear in any subsets.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
